<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 8501 0 R/Alt(Flux, in units of the continuum flux, against the Doppler velocity in units of the terminal velocity of the wind, from -1.5 to 1.5. The continuum is a dashed horizontal line at 1. On the blue side, between -1 and 0, the flux drops well below the continuum in an absorption trough, which ends sharply at -1. On the red side there is an emission peak, about 1.5 times the continuum just above zero velocity, which decreases to the continuum at +1.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[0]/Pg 21799 0 R>>
endobj
