8699 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 8700 0 R/Alt(Curves of v over c_iso against r over r_c, from 0 to 4, for different values of the integration constant. Two critical solutions cross at r = r_c, v = c_iso, marked by a dot. The wind, a thick black line, starts subsonic near the star, accelerates, becomes supersonic at r_c, and keeps accelerating slowly. The accretion solution, a thick red dashed line, is subsonic at large radii and supersonic inside r_c. Thin grey curves show the other solutions: some are subsonic everywhere, with a maximum of v at r_c; some are supersonic everywhere, with a minimum of v at r_c; others are double valued, either at small radii, where the velocity reaches c_iso with an infinite slope before r_c, or at large radii, where they never reach r_c.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[231]/Pg 21803 0 R>>
endobj
